    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0422" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1514.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-12T09:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1915—9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Collett recommends that credit order 1334 covering road to La Vega from Santo
                    Domingo submitted last year be now approved to the extent of two hundred
                    thousand dollars so that this work, first part of which is well under way, can
                    be rushed. We both consider this road the most important work on the island.
                    Bordas Government, and Minister of Fomento Velasquez now claim this credit order
                    is legal and requested Coilett to recommend its approval. I concur in this
                    recommendation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
